{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Summary\n\nGerrit Verified jobs fetch the exact patchset from Gerrit before any patchset code runs. During autodeploy/Gerrit contention windows this checkout can fail with a transient transport error (for example HTTP 504), and the old workflow let that first transport failure terminate the job. The resulting Verified -1 was a false code verdict because CI had not evaluated the change.\n\nOperator ruling recorded 2026-09-06/07 rejected Verified-0-on-fault and CI concurrency groups. The approved mitigation is in-job step-level retry for transport operations so transient Gerrit/autodeploy faults recover inside the same CI job and the final vote reflects real code status.\n\n## RCA\n\nThe failure is in the Gerrit patchset checkout operation, not in repository code. The affected workflows use `lfreleng-actions/checkout-gerrit-change-action` to fetch `refs/changes/*`; a transport failure there aborts the route before lint, tests, mutation, or other gates run. Retrying the checkout step locally in the job is the narrow portable seam: it targets the observable transport operation, avoids queue-wide serialization, and does not let patchset code influence vote logic.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [x] Every Gerrit Verified-lane patchset checkout has three in-job attempts: initial checkout, a 15 second retry, and a final 45 second retry.\n- [x] Retry attempts preserve the exact Gerrit inputs (`gerrit-refspec`, `gerrit-project`, `gerrit-url`) so the gate still checks out the requested patchset and does not replace it with a destructive manual ref operation.\n- [x] The retry is implemented inside the job step sequence rather than by casting Verified 0, adding CI concurrency groups, or touching infrastructure/Terraform.\n- [x] The retry mechanism is covered by a structural regression test that failed on the previous workflow shape and passes after the fix.\n- [x] Validation evidence exists: targeted workflow tests pass, lint/typecheck/mechanism/complexity ratchets pass, the known GIT_CONFIG isolation artifact passes solo with GIT_CONFIG_* unset, and full `make verify` passes with GIT_CONFIG_* unset."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1788851412153486001,"uuid":"eb92069f-76d8-40b4-a192-f0871bfd2bcf"}